      "side": 1,
      "message": "What are your thoughts on implementing this function as an `is_duplicate` fn as it was before, where instead of returning a bool, we return an int and the signature is something like:\n\n```\n/**\n * duplicate - Checks to see if the relocation entry has already been seen.\n *             If the entry hasn\u0027t been seen, it will be added to the relocation\n *             entries hashtable.\n * @elf64_rela_rht: The relocation entries hashtable\n * @rela: The relocation entry under test\n *\n * Return values:\n * 1: Indicates that the entry is a duplicate\n * 0: Indicates that the entry is not a duplicate\n * \u003c 0: Indicates that an error was encountered\n */\n static int duplicate(...)\n ```\n \n Note: You wouldn\u0027t actually add a comment to explain how the function works for a static function, but I did that for clarity.",
